# CELL 7b: PGRM INTEGRITY GATES   (Eir 2.0.13)
# ===========================================================================
# PGRM INTEGRITY GATES
#
# Four facets, asked in order. The first failure stops the assessment.
#
#   P  Parse      can the file be read?
#   G  Geometry   can the atoms be where it says?
#   R  Reference  can we assess it?
#   M  Model      is the depositor's description unambiguous?
#
# The point of the ordering is that a structure whose atoms cannot be where
# the file puts them has nothing to say about its chemistry. Eir previously
# decided severity FROM the bond valence sum, so a broken structure was judged
# by the number it produced: ICSD 220506 has a La-O contact of 1.008 A and
# reported a GII of 17.29 at the top of the triage; ICSD 85235 has two oxygens
# 0.56 A too close and reported a GII of 0.0047, the finest in the perovskite
# set. Both numbers are arithmetic performed on impossible coordinates.
#
# This replaces the six-type taxonomy of Reeves-McLaren (2026) Dalton Trans.
# 55, 2868, and contains it: Type 2 -> R1, Type 3 -> M1, Type 4 -> M3,
# Type 5 -> M2, Type 6A -> M6, Type 7 -> M4. Nothing is lost. What is added is
# the G facet, which that taxonomy had no category for and could not have had:
# it was derived on rock salts, where every atom sits on a special position
# with no free positional parameter, so a coordinate error is impossible by
# construction. Perovskites, pyrochlores and spinels all have positional
# freedom, and geometry faults are the dominant class in all three.
#
# Type 4 is implemented here for the first time. It was declared in 2016 and
# never assigned; the heterovalent test finds 3 pyrochlore and 309 spinel
# sites with a valence span of 2 or more on one Wyckoff position.
#
# PGRM_SUPPRESS controls whether an EXPUNGE actually withholds the chemistry.
# It ships False so the classification can be read for a run before it starts
# nulling columns, the same staging as 4a/4b.
# ===========================================================================
PGRM_SUPPRESS = False

# v2.0.22, item 4.1. Two thresholds for G6, and NEITHER IS MEASURED.
#
# They were chosen to sit clear of a test this project already built and
# rejected: 'is the shortest contact below the shortest ever observed for this
# ion' condemned 224 perovskite sites in sound structures, because Gagne's
# high-coordination configurations have small samples and their minimum is
# whatever the one unlucky entry happened to be.
#
# A margin below the minimum, on well-sampled configurations only, behaves
# completely differently. Measured across 3291 structures:
#
#     ratio < 1.00, any sample   perovskite  60   pyrochlore 131   spinel 107
#     ratio < 0.90, n >= 50      perovskite  17   pyrochlore   5   spinel   7
#
# 29 structures in total, 2 of them currently ACCEPT, and none of them
# marginal: Fe(3+) at 0.558 A against 65 measured FeO4 tetrahedra, Cr(3+) at
# 1.209 A against 104 measured CrO6 octahedra.
#
# Named so the choice is visible and can be moved. What IS measured is Gagne's
# minimum and its sample count; these two numbers are a reading of them.
MEASURED_MIN_RATIO = 0.90
MEASURED_MIN_SAMPLE = 50

# v2.0.36. THE POLYHEDRON IS THE WRONG SIZE FOR THE ION IN IT.
#
# bond_size_z is this site's mean bond length minus Gagne's mean for the same
# element, valence and coordination, in units of Gagne's OWN sd for that
# configuration. Scaled by the observed spread rather than by a percentage,
# because the spread runs from 1.2% of the bond for Sn(IV)O6 to 7.3% for
# Mn(III)O6 - a ninefold range, over which one fractional margin cannot serve.
#
# FITTED ON SOMETHING THAT IS NOT THE INDEX. A contracted polyhedron is
# over-bonded by construction, so fitting on gii would be fitting on
# arithmetic. The fit is on the rate at which an entry disagrees with every
# OTHER published determination of the same compound in the corpus, which uses
# neither bond valence nor Gagne. Over 1161 sites with at least three peers:
#
#     |z| bin      0-0.5  0.5-1  1-1.5  1.5-2  2-2.5  3-4   4+
#     outside all    13%    15%    16%    26%    52%  54%  47%
#
# The step is at 2 and holds at three to four times the base rate above it. On
# sites in structures carrying no code, 11% at |z| <= 1 against 83% above 3.
# Two-sided: too large is as wrong as too small, and the positive side behaves
# the same (21% of sites between 0 and +1 sit above 0.2 v.u., 97% beyond +4).
#
# ICSD 160115, Y2Sn2O7: six Sn-O at 1.946 A against 2.054 +/- 0.024, a bond
# valence sum of 6.00 against a formal 4, and six other determinations of the
# same compound between 2.024 and 2.104 A.
#
# 61 sites fire in 58 structures; the sound fraction moves 78.0 -> 74.2 on the
# pyrochlores, 74.9 -> 74.1 on the spinels and not at all on the perovskites.
# See Eir_bond_size_threshold.md for the per-family separation and the fit.
